# Contracts Integration
RULE: Use unified-api-contracts for external APIs (Databento, CCXT, Tardis). Import internal schemas (pubsub, lifecycle, features, ML, risk, events) from unified-internal-contracts only — never from unified_api_contracts.internal.
WHY: Type safety, VCR mocks for testing, canonical format normalization, contract validation; internal SSOT is UIC.
CODEX: 02-data/contracts-scope-and-layout.md, 05-infrastructure/contracts-integration.md, 02-data/vcr-cassette-ownership.md
DO: Import internal schemas from unified_internal_contracts; use unified-api-contracts for external + normalised; use VCR cassette path from unified-api-contracts (unified_api_contracts_external/<venue>/mocks/). VCR and live validation are done in the six interfaces (unified-market-interface, unified-trade-execution-interface, unified-sports-execution-interface, unified-reference-data-interface, unified-position-interface, unified-cloud-interface); they hold keys.

TYPED RESPONSE MODELS AT API BOUNDARIES:
  Every adapter that calls an external API MUST define Pydantic response models for that API's responses.
  Pattern: raw dict from response.json() → cast(dict[str, object], ...) → MyResponseModel.model_validate(raw)
  Then access typed attributes (model.field) instead of untyped dict access (raw["field"] or raw.get("field", {})).
  See: no-type-any-use-specific.mdc for full pattern and exemplars.
  Quality gates now BLOCK dict[str, Any] and raw response.json() without model_validate().

NEVER: from unified_api_contracts.internal import (use unified_internal_contracts); duplicate schema definitions; skip contract validation; hardcode API response parsing; use dict[str, Any] for API responses
